# Manual API requests for the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# A "Send Request" link appears above each request; click it to send the request.
# The response with status and timing opens on the right. Start `pnpm dev` first.
# Every endpoint with its body and answers is also described at http://localhost:3000/api/docs

@api = http://localhost:3000/api
@email = sofia@test.local
@password = secret123

### Health check: postgres and redis should be 'up'
GET {{api}}/health

### Sign-up → 201. The email comes back lowercased and trimmed
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "  sofia@Test.Local ",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Sofia"
}

### The same email again → 409
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Sofia"
}

### Validation errors → 400 with errors for each field
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123",
  "name": ""
}

### Malformed JSON → 400 before our pipe runs (Express rejects it)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "sofia@test.local",

### Login with a different email case → 200: accessToken and the user without the password hash.
# The refresh token comes in a cookie (see the Set-Cookie header in the response);
# REST Client remembers the cookie and sends it with later requests.
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "SOFIA@test.local",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Wrong password → 401. Compare the response time with the next request
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrong-pass"
}

### Unknown email → the same 401 in about the same time (dummy hash)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@test.local",
  "password": "wrong-pass"
}

# ——— Step 3: tokens. Send the "Login" request above (@name login) first ———

### Who am I → 200. The access token comes from the login response
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Who am I without a token → 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Who am I with a corrupted token → 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}x

### Refresh → 200, a new access token and a new refresh cookie (the old one no longer works)
# @name refresh
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh

### Who am I with the token from the refresh → 200
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.accessToken}}

### Logout → 204, the cookie is cleared
POST {{api}}/auth/logout

### Refresh after logout → 401
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh

# ——— Step 4: families. Send "Login" (@name login) again first ———

### Create a family → 201, I am a parent in it. Again → 201, another family: a person can be in several
# @name createFamily
POST {{api}}/families
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Ivanov family"
}

### My families → 200, an array, oldest membership first. The invites below use the first one
# @name myFamilies
GET {{api}}/families
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### The family with its members → 200. The id comes from the create response
GET {{api}}/families/{{createFamily.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Someone else's or a missing family → 404 (not 403: we don't reveal that the family exists)
GET {{api}}/families/7b1d3f8e-1a2b-4c3d-8e9f-0a1b2c3d4e5f
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Not a UUID → 400
GET {{api}}/families/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Empty name → 400
POST {{api}}/families
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}

# ─── Invites ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A parent creates a one-time link; a second user previews and accepts it.
# The family id comes from "My families" above, so send that request first.

@kidEmail = kid@test.local

### Create an invite → 201. The token is shown only here: the database keeps its hash
# @name createInvite
POST {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "child",
  "expiresInDays": 7
}

### Wrong role and lifetime → 400 with errors for both fields
POST {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "boss",
  "expiresInDays": 5
}

### The family's invites that still work → 200, without tokens
GET {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Second user: sign up (201, or 409 if they already exist), then log in
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{kidEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Kid"
}

###
# @name kid
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{kidEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Preview as the second user → 200: family, who invites, role, expiry, alreadyMember: false
GET {{api}}/invites/{{createInvite.response.body.token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{kid.response.body.accessToken}}

### Accept → 200, the family with the new member. Already in this family → 409
POST {{api}}/invites/{{createInvite.response.body.token}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{kid.response.body.accessToken}}

### The same link again → 404: it was one-time. Unknown, revoked and expired links get the same 404
POST {{api}}/invites/{{createInvite.response.body.token}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{kid.response.body.accessToken}}

### Revoke an invite → 204 (create a new one first: a used invite can't be revoked, → 404)
DELETE {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/invites/{{createInvite.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

# ─── Boards ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any member of the family manages boards (roles come in stage 3).
# The family id comes from "My families" above, so send that request first.
# Got 401? The access token lives 15 minutes: send "Login" (# @name login) above again.

### Create a board → 201, with the columns "To do", "In progress", "Done" (positions a0, a1, a2)
# @name createBoard
POST {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/boards
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Home"
}

### The family's boards → 200, oldest first
GET {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/boards
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### One board with its columns and cards → 200
GET {{api}}/boards/{{createBoard.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Rename → 200
PATCH {{api}}/boards/{{createBoard.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Home chores"
}

### A missing board, or a board of a family I'm not in → the same 404
GET {{api}}/boards/7b1d3f8e-1a2b-4c3d-8e9f-0a1b2c3d4e5f
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Delete → 204, with its columns and cards. Again → 404
DELETE {{api}}/boards/{{createBoard.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

# ─── Columns and cards ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A board of its own, because the Boards section above ends by deleting its board.
# Order is stored as fractional-indexing keys; the server computes them, the client only says
# "after this card" (or null for first).

### A board for this section → 201, with the columns "To do", "In progress", "Done"
# @name cardsBoard
POST {{api}}/families/{{myFamilies.response.body.$[0].id}}/boards
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Chores"
}

### Add a column → 201, at the end of the board
# @name newColumn
POST {{api}}/boards/{{cardsBoard.response.body.id}}/columns
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someday"
}

### Rename the column → 200
PATCH {{api}}/columns/{{newColumn.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Later"
}

### Move the column first → 200, a key before "a0" (afterColumnId: another column's id puts it after that one)
POST {{api}}/columns/{{newColumn.response.body.id}}/move
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "afterColumnId": null
}

### Add a card to "To do" → 201, at the end of the column. Only the title is required
# @name card1
POST {{api}}/columns/{{cardsBoard.response.body.columns[0].id}}/cards
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Buy milk"
}

### A card with every field → 201. The assignee must be a member of the family (else 400);
### the due date is ISO 8601, YYYY-MM-DD (else 400)
# @name card2
POST {{api}}/columns/{{cardsBoard.response.body.columns[0].id}}/cards
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Homework",
  "description": "Math, page 12",
  "assigneeId": "{{login.response.body.user.id}}",
  "dueDate": "2026-11-30"
}

### Change only the due date → 200, the other fields stay. null clears assigneeId or dueDate
PATCH {{api}}/cards/{{card2.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dueDate": "2026-12-01"
}

### Move "Homework" first in "To do" → 200, a key before the first card
POST {{api}}/cards/{{card2.response.body.id}}/move
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "columnId": "{{cardsBoard.response.body.columns[0].id}}",
  "afterCardId": null
}

### Move "Buy milk" to "In progress" → 200. afterCardId must be a card of the target column (else 409)
POST {{api}}/cards/{{card1.response.body.id}}/move
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "columnId": "{{cardsBoard.response.body.columns[1].id}}",
  "afterCardId": null
}

### The board now: columns and cards in order → 200
GET {{api}}/boards/{{cardsBoard.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Delete a column that still has cards → 409 "Move or delete the cards first"
DELETE {{api}}/columns/{{cardsBoard.response.body.columns[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Delete a card → 204. Again → 404
DELETE {{api}}/cards/{{card2.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Delete the empty column → 204
DELETE {{api}}/columns/{{newColumn.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
